=6. So digits are 9,3,4,7,6 and U=2. All unique. Similarly, the second case: 9,3,6,7,4 and U=2. All unique. So both are valid. Therefore, U=2 is possible.\n\nCase 2: A=4, D=6\n\nThen S=10, T=10. So again, N + E=10. Available digits: U=2, \u041b=9, A=4, D=6. So remaining digits: 0,1,3,5,7,8.\n\nNeed N + E=10. Possible pairs:\n\n0 +10 invalid\n\n1 +9=10, 9 is used.\n\n3 +7=10\n\n5 +5=10 invalid\n\n7 +3=10\n\n8 +2=10, 2 is used.\n\nSo possible pairs (3,7) and (7,3). Let's check if these digits are available.\n\nIf N=3, E=7: digits used are U=2, \u041b=9, A=4, D=6, N=3, E=7. All unique. Remaining digits 0,1,5,8. Okay. Then \u041b\u0410\u041d is 943, \u0414\u042d=67. 943 +67=1010. 943 +67=1010. Correct. Similarly, if N=7, E=3: \u041b\u0410\u041d=947, \u0414\u042d=63. 947 +63=1010. 947 +63=1010. Correct. Digits: 9,4,7,6,3. All unique. So U=2 is possible here as well.\n\nCase 3: A=6, D=4\n\nThen S=10, T=10. N + E=10. Available digits: U=2, \u041b=9, A=6, D=4. Remaining digits: 0,1,3,5,7,8.\n\nPossible pairs for N + E=10:\n\n0 +10 invalid\n\n1 +9=10, 9 is used.\n\n3 +7=10\n\n5 +5=10 invalid\n\n7 +3=10\n\n8 +2=10, 2 is used.\n\nSo again, pairs (3,7) and (7,3). Let's check:\n\nIf N=3, E=7: \u041b\u0410\u041d=963, \u0414\u042d=47. 963 +47=1010. 963 +47=1010. Correct. Digits:9,6,3,4,7. All unique. If N=7, E=3: \u041b\u0410\u041d=967, \u0414\u042d=43. 967 +43=1010. Correct. Digits:9,6,7,4,3. All unique. So U=2 is possible here too.\n\nCase 4: A=7, D=3\n\nThen S=10, T=10. N + E=10. Available digits: U=2, \u041b=9, A=7, D=3. Remaining digits: 0,1,4,5,6,8.\n\nPossible pairs for N + E=10:\n\n0 +10 invalid\n\n1 +9=10, 9 is used.\n\n4 +6=10\n\n5 +5=10 invalid\n\n6 +4=10\n\n8 +2=10, 2 is used.\n\nSo pairs (4,6) and (6,4). For example, N=4, E=6: \u041b\u0410\u041d=974, \u0414\u042d=36. 974 +36=1010. Correct. Digits:9,7,4,3,6. All unique. Or N=6, E=4: \u041b\u0410\u041d=976, \u0414\u042d=34. 976 +34=1010. Correct. Digits:9,7,6,3,4. All unique. So again, valid.\n\nTherefore, for U=2, ther