sine of the angle formed by $EM$ and $AN$.\n\n**Steps:**\n\n1. Notice that $\\triangle ABC$ is an equilateral triangle and $A B D E$ is a square. Let \\( AB = 2 \\).\n2. Construct the geometry such that $O$ and $F$ are the midpoints of $AB$ and $DE$, respectively.\n3. Calculate $OF$ (the distance between midpoints of $AB$ and $DE$), $OB$, and $OC$:\n   \\[\n   OF = 2, \\quad OB = 1, \\quad OC = \\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate the vector expressions:\n   \\[\n   \\overrightarrow{AN} = \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\overrightarrow{ON} = \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\frac{1}{2} (\\overrightarrow{OB} + \\overrightarrow{OC})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\overrightarrow{AN} = \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{AB} + \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\overrightarrow{OB} + \\overrightarrow{OC} \\right) = \\frac{3}{2} \\overrightarrow{OB} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OC}\n   \\]\n\n5. Similarly, compute $\\overrightarrow{EM}$:\n   \\[\n   \\overrightarrow{EM} = \\overrightarrow{EA} + \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\overrightarrow{OM} = \\overrightarrow{EA} + \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\frac{1}{2} (\\overrightarrow{OA} + \\overrightarrow{OC})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\overrightarrow{EM} = -\\overrightarrow{OF} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OB} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OC}\n   \\]\n\n6. Calculate the dot product $\\overrightarrow{AN} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{EM}$:\n   \\[\n   \\overrightarrow{AN} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{EM} = \\left( \\frac{3}{2} \\overrightarrow{OB} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OC} \\right) \\cdot \\left( -\\overrightarrow{OF} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OB} + \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OC} \\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{OC} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{OF} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n7. Compute magnitudes:\n   \\[\n   |\\overrightarrow{AN}| = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{3}{2} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9}